#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""cc-subject — an experiment's subject in a sandbox of its own, whose only way out is the model API.

A member workspace runs experiments whose subjects are headless Claude sessions using Bash. Inside the workspace a
subject would see the whole workspace and the whole network, and a command denylist is no wall: a raw socket walks past
it. So the HOST starts each subject in its own bwrap, and the subject's world is:
  /work           a tmpfs of SUBJECT_DISK_MB, rw: empty, or holding a copy of one directory of the workspace (--in).
                  That directory is measured first (st_blocks of everything in it, through the descriptor it was opened
                  with, no link followed) and refused if it takes more than SUBJECT_DISK_MB; then it is copied on the
                  host, inside a second bwrap that sees only it, into the run's in/, which is measured while it fills
                  and after, so a source that grows meanwhile is stopped too. in/ is bound read-only at /in, and the
                  sandbox's own first process copies /in into /work, so an input too big for /work fails the run. The
                  kernel counts every page, an unlinked file still open included, and a write past the size gets ENOSPC.
  /home/subject   HOME, a 512 MB tmpfs (HOME_BYTES), holding no credential at all; it is not kept after the run
  /usr, /etc      the distribution, ro; /etc is a tmpfs holding the loader cache, the CA certs and a generated passwd
  the network     NONE of its own: an empty network namespace whose only interface is loopback. 127.0.0.1:3128 is a
                  forwarder to a unix socket the host serves, and that is the model API as far as the subject knows:
                  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL names it, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is a placeholder, and no proxy variable is set.
                  A raw socket to anywhere has no route.
  limits          a user systemd scope of its own, cc-subject-<run>.scope (MemoryMax, MemorySwapMax=0, TasksMax; the
                  tmpfs pages count against MemoryMax), a size-capped /tmp and a per-file size limit
Absent, not denied: the workspace and its tracks, ~/.cc, the host's home, every credential. No host firewall rule,
interface or routing table is touched: the namespace is the subject's, and only bwrap makes it.

THE END of a run, whatever ends it (the subject exits, stop, the hours, a cap, an error in the supervisor): the
sandbox's first process does not exit with the subject but reports "exit N" on a pipe and waits, so /work is still
there. The supervisor freezes the scope's cgroup and counts the entries in /work: past WORK_ENTRIES (100000) nothing
is copied, because an empty file costs the tmpfs nothing but costs the host an inode. The count walks each dir
from its parent's fd O_NOFOLLOW and enters no link; a dir it cannot open or list (EMFILE on a deep chain too)
means nothing is copied, never a subtree skipped. The --in and kept-results size caps and the `status RUN` listing
use the same walk, so a dir they cannot read refuses the cap and a link is listed as a link, never stat'd through
(an absolute link in a live /work would resolve on the host). Otherwise it copies
/proc/<sandbox>/root/work out to the run's work/ (a link is copied as a link, never followed), makes every copied dir 0700 and file 0600 (0700 if it was executable) with no
set-id bit, then kills the cgroup. A scope that does not confirm it is frozen is killed with nothing copied. While a run
is live, `status` reads its /work through /proc, after checking the process is still in the run's own scope.
Ended runs older than SUBJECT_KEEP_DAYS (14) lose work/, in/ and home/ the next time the workspace starts a run, and
ledger files older than that are deleted; status.json and the logs stay. The same sweep removes the in/ of every run
that is not live, whatever its age, so a launcher killed in the middle of a copy leaves nothing behind for long. All a
workspace keeps under subjects/<h> is capped at SUBJECT_KEPT_MB (8192), counted in st_blocks but at least ENTRY_BYTES
(4 KB) an entry, with no link followed: past it no run starts, and that refusal is not one of the day's runs.

THE PROXY is a reverse proxy, not a tunnel. It lets through POST /v1/messages (priced) and /v1/messages/count_tokens
(free), with no query or `beta=true`, and answers 403 to everything else: CONNECT, GET, any other path, an absolute
URL. A request needs a Content-Length (chunked is refused), a head under HEAD_MAX and a body under BODY_MAX that
parses as a JSON object, with no key twice in any object, without mcp_servers, container or inference_geo and without server tools (a tool's type is
custom or a client tool's). The proxy drops the subject's own auth, cookie, encoding and hop-by-hop headers, reads the
workspace's access token from its credentials.json on every request (O_NOFOLLOW, so a refresh is picked up and a
planted link gets a 503), and sends the request on over HTTPS to UPSTREAM with that token, one request a connection.

CAPS, per workspace and per UTC day of a run's start: SUBJECT_DAILY_USD dollars (10),
SUBJECT_DAILY_NET_MB megabytes through the proxy (1024), SUBJECT_MAX_HOURS per run (6; a run that names none gets 2,
or the cap if lower), SUBJECT_CONCURRENT at once (2), SUBJECT_KEPT_MB kept on disk (8192) — `cc-config set` changes
them. How many runs a day start is not capped: the dollars are. A run charges the
ledger of the UTC day it started, however long it goes on. Dollars and bytes are both kept by the proxy, the
subject's only way out, in ONE ledger per workspace and day (subjects/<h>/ledger/<day>.json, edited under a flock),
which every run of that workspace shares, so two runs at once cannot each spend what is left:
  dollars   before a priced request goes out the proxy asks the API's free count_tokens for its input (the body cut
            to COUNT_KEYS, the same login) and holds its worst case R (hold_terms(): that count plus 2% and 1024, or,
            if the count fails, every byte of the body a token and documents and URLs a full context; cache writes at
            their dearest; all of max_tokens out; the model's dearest row, a model with no row at the dearest of all;
            twice that past 200k input). It settles R from the usage the API sends back (cc-spend's rates). A stream
            cut before message_stop, or a subject that hangs up before the answer, settles at R or what it saw,
            if more; an error status settles at 0. A request
            whose R fits once other requests settle waits up to WAIT_MAX seconds, then gets a 429. One that would not
            fit even with nothing in flight goes out with max_tokens cut to the most that fits now (the body
            re-encoded, its Content-Length with it), since the answer cannot run past max_tokens; if that cut would
            reach its thinking budget it gets a 429 instead. Only when not even max_tokens 1 fits beside what is
            settled is the day spent: a 403, and the run is killed. Holds a run leaves open are settled at R when it
            ends.
  bytes     every byte relayed, both ways, the proxy's own count_tokens calls included, taken from the day's ledger
            in blocks before it is sent; the unused part of a block goes back when the run ends. Past the cap the run is killed. Bytes are a backstop for what
            dollars do not see (free calls, error answers); dollars are the cap.
A ledger that will not read is a refusal, never a zero.

usage, INSIDE a member workspace (the request crosses the workspace's own Slack socket as the member verb `subject`):
  cc-subject run [--in DIR] [--hours H] -- CMD [ARGS...]   start CMD in a new subject sandbox; prints the run id
  cc-subject stop RUN                                       end a run of this workspace's
  cc-subject status [RUN [PATH]]                            no RUN: this workspace's runs. RUN: its state, the tails of
                                                            out.log and net.log, and what is under its /work. PATH: one
                                                            regular file under that /work, up to READ_BYTES of it
  The results stay on the host (~/.cc/members/<handle>/subjects/<run>/); the workspace reads them only through
  `status`, so nothing the subject wrote is ever bound into the workspace. status.json records when the
  workspace's login expires (login_expires), and `status RUN` says so, since calls made after that get a 401.
  The proxy's socket sits in a short host-only dir ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cc-subject/<hash>, else ~/.cc/s/<hash>), so a long handle cannot push its path
  past the 107 bytes a unix socket allows.
usage, on the host:
  cc-subject launch <handle>          the daemon's door: one JSON ask on stdin ({"op": "run", "argv": [...],
                                      "input": DIR, "hours": H}, {"op": "stop", "run": RUN} or {"op": "status",
                                      "run": RUN, "path": PATH}, run and path optional), one JSON answer out
  cc-subject list <handle>
  cc-subject supervise <handle> <run> private: the detached runner launch starts
  cc-subject selfcheck
"""
import calendar
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import http.client
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import re
import runpy
import secrets
import select
import shutil
import signal
import socket
import ssl
import stat
import subprocess as sp
import sys
import threading
import time
import traceback

BIN = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REALHOME = Path(os.path.expanduser("~"))
# Only the selfcheck moves this: it names where the member dirs and the workspace trees are read from, never the
# boundary's shape. The daemon that calls `launch` runs with the host's own environment, which no member sets.
HOME = Path(os.environ.get("CC_SUBJECT_HOME") or REALHOME)
# (host, port, tls): where the proxy sends what it lets through. Only the selfcheck moves it, to a plain-HTTP fake.
UPSTREAM = ("api.anthropic.com", 443, True)
API_PATHS = {"/v1/messages": True, "/v1/messages/count_tokens": False}   # the only paths out, and whether priced
API_QUERIES = ("", "beta=true")
HEAD_MAX, BODY_MAX = 16 << 10, 32 << 20      # a request's head and body
MAX_TOKENS = 1_000_000                       # a max_tokens past this is refused, not reserved
TOKEN = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{1,4096}")   # what an access token may be before it goes into a header
OAUTH_BETA = "oauth-2025-04-20"
FORBID_KEYS = ("mcp_servers", "container", "inference_geo")
TOOL_TYPE = re.compile(r"custom|(bash|text_editor|computer|memory)_\d{8}")   # client tools; server tools are refused
DOC_TYPES = ("document", "container_upload", "url", "file")
# What the proxy sends to count_tokens of a priced request's body, and the margin it adds to the count it gets back:
# the API calls that count an estimate, and the hold must stay the worst case.
COUNT_KEYS = ("model", "messages", "system", "tools", "tool_choice", "thinking")
COUNT_TIMEOUT = 30
WAIT_MAX, WAIT_STEP = 120.0, 0.5             # how long a request waits for in-flight ones to settle, then 429
BYTES_BLOCK = 1 << 20                        # bytes are taken from the day's ledger this many at a time
UP_TIMEOUT = 600
SEARCH_USD = 0.01                            # per web search the usage reports
PROXY_PORT = 3128
TICK = 5.0
COPY_WAIT = 300
WORK_ENTRIES = 100_000         # a /work holding more entries than this is not copied out at all
ENTRY_BYTES = 4096             # what every entry costs the kept cap at least: an empty file takes an inode, not a block
CRED_MARGIN = 15 * 60          # a login closer than this to expiry cannot start a run
HANDLE = re.compile(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,62}")
RUN = re.compile(r"\d{8}-\d{6}-[0-9a-f]{6}")
DEFAULTS = {"SUBJECT_DAILY_USD": 10.0, "SUBJECT_MAX_HOURS": 6.0, "SUBJECT_CONCURRENT": 2,
            "SUBJECT_DISK_MB": 1024, "SUBJECT_DAILY_NET_MB": 1024.0, "SUBJECT_KEEP_DAYS": 14, "SUBJECT_KEPT_MB": 8192}
# Where the proxy's socket dir goes: short and host-only, whatever the handle. Only the selfcheck moves it.
RUNTIME = os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") or None
MEMORY, TASKS = "4G", 512      # the scope's MemoryMax (tmpfs pages count against it) and TasksMax
SUPERVISOR_MEMORY = "2G"       # the supervisor's own scope: it parses request bodies, up to 16 at once
TMP_BYTES = 512 << 20          # /tmp inside
HOME_BYTES = 512 << 20         # /home/subject inside; with /work and /tmp it leaves ~2 GB of MEMORY to the processes
FREEZE_WAIT = 10.0             # how long the end waits for the scope to report itself frozen
INFO_WAIT = 60.0               # how long the supervisor waits for bwrap to name the sandbox's pid
FILE_BYTES = 1 << 30           # RLIMIT_FSIZE: no single file, out.log included, past this
NET_LOG_LINES = 5000           # net.log stops here, with one line saying so
READ_BYTES = 256 << 10         # `status RUN PATH` hands back at most this much of one file
TAIL_LINES, LIST_MAX = 40, 200 # `status RUN`: lines of each log, entries of /work
LIVE = ("starting", "running")


def now():
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())


def today():
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d", time.gmtime())


def member_dir(h):
    return HOME / ".cc/members" / h


def subjects(h):
    return member_dir(h) / "subjects"


def sock_dir(h, run):
    """The run's own dir for the proxy's socket: <base>/<16 hex of handle and run>, where <base> is
    $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cc-subject or else ~/.cc/s — a few dozen bytes whatever the handle, under the 107 a unix
    socket path may hold. Nothing a member or subject writes is on either path."""
    base = Path(RUNTIME) / "cc-subject" if RUNTIME else HOME / ".cc/s"
    return base / hashlib.sha256(f"{h}/{run}".encode()).hexdigest()[:16]


def make_sock_dir(d):
    """Make `d` (and its base) 0700, refusing a base that is a link or not this user's."""
    d.parent.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    st = os.lstat(d.parent)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or st.st_uid != os.getuid():
        raise OSError(f"{d.parent} is not a directory of this user's")
    os.chmod(d.parent, 0o700)
    d.mkdir(mode=0o700)
    return d


def config(key):
    d = DEFAULTS[key]
    try:
        v = sp.run([str(BIN / "cc-config"), "get", key, str(d)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10).stdout.strip()
        return type(d)(v)
    except (OSError, ValueError, sp.SubprocessError):
        return d


def caps():
    return {k: config(k) for k in DEFAULTS}


def read_json(p, default=None):
    try:
        with open(p) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return default


def write_json(p, obj):
    tmp = Path(f"{p}.{os.getpid()}.{threading.get_ident()}.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=1) + "\n")
    os.replace(tmp, p)


def runs_of(h):
    """(run id, status) for every run of a workspace, oldest first."""
    root = subjects(h)
    out = []
    for d in sorted(root.iterdir()) if root.is_dir() else []:
        if RUN.fullmatch(d.name):
            st = read_json(d / "status.json")
            if isinstance(st, dict):
                out.append((d.name, st))
    return out


def alive(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(int(pid), 0)
        return True
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):   # gone, or a pid now another user's: not this run's supervisor
        return False


def state_of(st):
    """A run's state, where one marked live whose supervisor process is gone is `failed`: nothing will ever end it,
    and bwrap --die-with-parent took the subject down with that supervisor."""
    s = st.get("state")
    return "failed" if s in LIVE and not alive(st.get("supervisor")) else s


def day_totals(h, day):
    """Runs started on `day` (UTC, the YYYY-MM-DD of their start stamp), every one of them, a run whose input copy
    failed included, and how many of the workspace's runs are live. Dollars and bytes are the ledger's."""
    every = runs_of(h)
    live = sum(1 for _, st in every if state_of(st) in LIVE)
    return sum(1 for _, st in every if str(st.get("started", ""))[:10] == day), live


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the credential (host side only)

def read_login(p):
    """The `claudeAiOauth` dict of the credentials file `p`, or None. The file is opened O_NOFOLLOW and must be a
    regular file: a link planted in its place is no login."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(p, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError:
        return None
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):
            return None
        raw = f.read(1 << 16)
    try:
        oauth = json.loads(raw).get("claudeAiOauth")
    except (ValueError, RecursionError, AttributeError):
        return None
    return oauth if isinstance(oauth, dict) else None


def read_token(p):
    """The access token in `p`, read afresh (so a refresh the workspace made is used), or None if it is not one."""
    oauth = read_login(p)
    tok = oauth.get("accessToken") if oauth else None
    return tok if isinstance(tok, str) and TOKEN.fullmatch(tok) else None


def login_why(h):
    """None if workspace `h` has a login a run can use, else why not. The subject never holds it: the proxy does."""
    oauth = read_login(member_dir(h) / "credentials.json")
    if not oauth or not isinstance(oauth.get("accessToken"), str) or not TOKEN.fullmatch(oauth["accessToken"]):
        return f"workspace {h} has no login of its own, so a subject has nothing to call the API with"
    exp = oauth.get("expiresAt")
    if isinstance(exp, (int, float)) and exp / 1000 < time.time() + CRED_MARGIN:
        return (f"workspace {h}'s login expires within {CRED_MARGIN // 60} minutes; any session in the workspace "
                "renews it, so start one and ask again")
    return None


def login_expires(h):
    """When workspace `h`'s access token expires (a UTC stamp), or None if its login does not say. The proxy reads the
    token afresh on every call, so a renewal moves this; a run records it so the member can see why calls get a 401."""
    oauth = read_login(member_dir(h) / "credentials.json")
    exp = oauth.get("expiresAt") if oauth else None
    if type(exp) not in (int, float):
        return None
    try:
        return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(exp / 1000))
    except (OverflowError, OSError, ValueError):
        return None


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the day's ledger, shared by every run

class LedgerError(Exception):
    pass


class Ledger:
    """One workspace's dollars and proxy bytes for one UTC day: {"usd": settled, "held": {run/seq: R in flight},
    "bytes": taken}. Every edit is made under a flock on subjects/<h>/.ledger.lock (taken after .lock when both are),
    so the runs of a workspace — other processes, or threads of this one — share one figure. A file that is there but
    will not read is a LedgerError, and every caller refuses on it: a broken ledger is never a zero."""

    def __init__(self, h, day):
        self.dir = subjects(h) / "ledger"
        self.path = self.dir / f"{day}.json"
        self.lock_path = subjects(h) / ".ledger.lock"

    def load(self):
        try:
            fd = os.open(self.path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            return {"usd": 0.0, "held": {}, "bytes": 0}
        except OSError as e:
            raise LedgerError(f"the day's ledger will not open: {e.strerror}") from None
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
            raw = f.read(4 << 20)
        try:
            d = json.loads(raw)
        except (ValueError, RecursionError):
            raise LedgerError("the day's ledger is not JSON") from None
        ok = (isinstance(d, dict) and type(d.get("usd")) in (int, float) and d["usd"] >= 0
              and type(d.get("bytes")) is int and d["bytes"] >= 0 and isinstance(d.get("held"), dict)
              and all(type(v) in (int, float) and v >= 0 for v in d["held"].values()))
        if not ok:
            raise LedgerError("the day's ledger does not hold what a ledger holds")
        return d

    @contextlib.contextmanager
    def edit(self):
        self.dir.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(self.lock_path, "a") as lk:
            fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            d = self.load()
            before = json.dumps(d, sort_keys=True)
            yield d
            if json.dumps(d, sort_keys=True) != before:
                write_json(self.path, d)

    def read(self):
        with self.edit() as d:
            return {"usd": d["usd"], "held": dict(d["held"]), "bytes": d["bytes"]}

    def hold(self, key, fixed, per_out, mt, floor, cap):
        """Hold the worst case of request `key`, fixed + max_tokens * per_out, asked at max_tokens `mt`. Returns
        (verdict, max_tokens held):
          ("ok", mt)    it fits beside what is settled and what is in flight;
          ("ok", m)     it does not fit even with nothing in flight, but at max_tokens m (floor <= m < mt) it fits now;
          ("wait", 0)   it would fit whole (or at all, past `floor`) once what is in flight settles;
          ("short", 0)  no max_tokens from `floor` up fits even then: a 429, the day is not spent;
          ("over", 0)   not even max_tokens 1 fits beside what is settled: the day is spent."""
        def fit(room):
            if room < fixed + per_out:
                return 0
            m = min(mt, int((room - fixed) / per_out))
            while m > 0 and fixed + m * per_out > room:
                m -= 1
            return m
        floor = min(floor, mt)
        with self.edit() as d:
            room_set = cap - d["usd"]
            room_all = room_set - sum(d["held"].values())
            if fixed + per_out > room_set:
                return "over", 0
            fa, fs = fit(room_all), fit(room_set)
            if fa < mt and fs >= mt:
                return "wait", 0
            if fa < floor:
                return ("wait" if fs >= floor else "short"), 0
            d["held"][key] = fixed + fa * per_out
            return "ok", fa

    def settle(self, key, usd):
        """Replace the hold `key` with what the request cost; False, and nothing added, if the hold is gone."""
        with self.edit() as d:
            if d["held"].pop(key, None) is None:
                return False
            d["usd"] += usd
            return True

    def release_run(self, run):
        """Settle every hold run `run` left open at its R, and return their sum."""
        with self.edit() as d:
            mine = [k for k in d["held"] if k.startswith(run + "/")]
            got = sum(d["held"].pop(k) for k in mine)
            d["usd"] += got
            return got

    def take_bytes(self, need, cap):
        """Take a BYTES_BLOCK from the day's bytes (`need` if more), or just `need` if a block will not fit; how many
        were taken, 0 when not even `need` fits."""
        with self.edit() as d:
            room = cap - d["bytes"]
            got = max(need, BYTES_BLOCK)
            got = got if got <= room else need if need <= room else 0
            d["bytes"] += got
            return got

    def give_bytes(self, n):
        if n:
            with self.edit() as d:
                d["bytes"] = max(0, d["bytes"] - n)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ prices

_SPEND = None


def spend():
    global _SPEND
    if _SPEND is None:
        _SPEND = runpy.run_path(str(BIN / "cc-spend"))
    return _SPEND


def worst_rates(model):
    """(input, output) $ per M tokens for a reservation: the dearer of the model's normal and fast rows; a model with
    no row gets the dearest of every row."""
    s = spend()
    rows = [r for r in (s["rate"](model), s["rate"](model, True)) if r]
    if not rows:
        rows = list(s["RATES"].values()) + list(s["FAST"].values())
    return max(r[0] for r in rows), max(r[1] for r in rows)


def price(model, u):
    """One usage block in dollars with cc-spend's rates. A model with no row is priced at the dearest row there is."""
    s = spend()
    fast = u.get("speed") == "fast"
    v = s["usd"](model, u, fast)
    if v is None:
        v = max(s["usd"](m, u, f) for m in s["RATES"] for f in (False, True))
    return v


def cost(model, u):
    """What a response's usage costs: its price (or the sum of its iterations', if more), twice that past 200k input
    tokens, and SEARCH_USD a web search."""
    v = price(model, u)
    it = u.get("iterations")
    if isinstance(it, list):
        v = max(v, sum(price(model, x) for x in it if isinstance(x, dict)))
    tin = sum(int(u.get(k) or 0) for k in ("input_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens", "cache_creation_input_tokens"))
    if tin > 200_000:
        v *= 2
    stu = u.get("server_tool_use")
    return v + SEARCH_USD * int((stu.get("web_search_requests") if isinstance(stu, dict) else 0) or 0)


def count_margin(n):
    """The input tokens a hold assumes for a request count_tokens put at `n`: 2% and 1024 more, since the API calls
    that count an estimate and a hold must be the worst case."""
    return n + n // 50 + 1024


def hold_terms(ask, nbytes, counted=None):
    """(fixed, per_out): the worst a request can cost before it is sent is fixed + max_tokens * per_out. Its input
    tokens are count_margin(counted) when count_tokens answered, else the body's own estimate: every body byte a
    token (plus a margin, and 10k a picture), a full context if it names a document, file or URL. Cache writes are at
    their dearest multiple, every token out at the model's dearest row, and the whole twice past 200k input tokens."""
    images, doc, cc, cc1h, stack = 0, False, False, False, [ask]
    while stack:
        x = stack.pop()
        if isinstance(x, dict):
            ty = x.get("type")
            images += ty == "image"
            doc = doc or ty in DOC_TYPES or "file_id" in x
            if "cache_control" in x:
                cc = True
                cc1h = cc1h or (isinstance(x["cache_control"], dict) and x["cache_control"].get("ttl") == "1h")
            stack.extend(x.values())
        elif isinstance(x, list):
            stack.extend(x)
    if counted is not None:
        tin = count_margin(counted)
    else:
        tin = 1_000_000 if doc else min(1_000_000, nbytes + 8192 + 10000 * images)
    mult = 2.0 if cc1h else 1.25 if cc else 1.0
    rin, rout = worst_rates(ask["model"])
    k = 2 if tin > 200_000 else 1
    return k * tin * rin * mult / 1e6, k * rout / 1e6


def reserve(ask, nbytes, counted=None):
    """The hold R for a request as it is: hold_terms at its own max_tokens."""
    fixed, per_out = hold_terms(ask, nbytes, counted)
    return fixed + int(ask.get("max_tokens") or 0) * per_out


def thinking_floor(ask):
    """The least max_tokens a request may be cut to: one past its thinking budget (the API refuses a max_tokens at or
    under it), else 1."""
    th = ask.get("thinking")
    b = th.get("budget_tokens") if isinstance(th, dict) and th.get("type") == "enabled" else None
    return b + 1 if type(b) is int and b >= 0 else 1


def vet(ask, priced):
    """None if the request body may go out, else why not."""
    if not isinstance(ask, dict):
        return "the body is not a JSON object"
    for k in FORBID_KEYS:
        if k in ask:
            return f"{k} does not go through this proxy"
    if not isinstance(ask.get("model"), str):
        return "the body names no model"
    tools = ask.get("tools", [])
    if not isinstance(tools, list):
        return "tools is not a list"
    for t in tools:
        if not isinstance(t, dict):
            return "a tool is not an object"
        ty = t.get("type")
        if ty is not None and not (isinstance(ty, str) and TOOL_TYPE.fullmatch(ty)):
            return f"tool type {str(ty)[:60]!r} does not go through this proxy: server tools are refused"
    mt = ask.get("max_tokens")
    if priced and (type(mt) is not int or not 0 < mt <= MAX_TOKENS):
        return f"max_tokens must be a whole number from 1 to {MAX_TOKENS}"
    return None


PARSE = threading.Lock()   # one body parsed at a time, so sixteen 32 MB bodies are never in the parser together


def unique(pairs):
    """An object with a key twice is no body: the proxy and the API could each read a different one of them."""
    d = dict(pairs)
    if len(d) != len(pairs):
        raise ValueError("a key twice")
    return d


def parse(raw):
    with PARSE:
        try:
            return json.loads(raw, object_pairs_hook=unique)
        except (ValueError, RecursionError, MemoryError):
            return None


class Usage:
    """The usage of one response, read as it is relayed: a JSON body whole, or an SSE stream's message_start usage
    merged with its message_delta usage, complete only once message_stop has been seen."""
    LINE_MAX = 1 << 20

    def __init__(self, sse):
        self.sse, self.buf, self.skip = sse, bytearray(), False
        self.u, self.model, self.complete = None, None, False

    def feed(self, d):
        if not self.sse:
            if self.buf is not None:
                self.buf += d
                if len(self.buf) > BODY_MAX:
                    self.buf = None   # too big to read: opaque, so it settles at R
            return
        self.buf += d
        while True:
            i = self.buf.find(b"\n")
            if i < 0:
                if len(self.buf) > self.LINE_MAX:   # a line this long is no usage event: drop it to its end
                    self.buf.clear()
                    self.skip = True
                return
            line = bytes(self.buf[:i]).rstrip(b"\r")
            del self.buf[:i + 1]
            if self.skip:
                self.skip = False
            elif line.startswith(b"data:"):
                self.event(parse(line[5:]))

    def event(self, ev):
        if not isinstance(ev, dict):
            return
        t = ev.get("type")
        if t == "message_start" and isinstance(ev.get("message"), dict):
            m = ev["message"]
            self.model = m.get("model") if isinstance(m.get("model"), str) else None
            if isinstance(m.get("usage"), dict):
                self.u = {k: v for k, v in m["usage"].items() if v is not None}
        elif t == "message_delta" and isinstance(ev.get("usage"), dict):
            self.u = {**(self.u or {}), **{k: v for k, v in ev["usage"].items() if v is not None}}
        elif t == "message_stop":
            self.complete = self.u is not None

    def finish(self):
        if self.sse or not self.buf:
            return
        j = parse(bytes(self.buf))
        if isinstance(j, dict) and isinstance(j.get("usage"), dict):
            self.u, self.complete = j["usage"], True
            self.model = j.get("model") if isinstance(j.get("model"), str) else None

    def usd(self, model):
        """(dollars, complete) — dollars None when there is no usage, or it will not price."""
        if self.u is None:
            return None, False
        try:
            return float(cost(self.model or model, self.u)), self.complete
        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError, OverflowError):
            return None, False


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the proxy (host side)

STRIP = frozenset({"authorization", "x-api-key", "cookie", "accept-encoding", "expect", "host", "content-length",
                   "connection", "keep-alive", "proxy-connection", "proxy-authorization", "proxy-authenticate", "te",
                   "trailer", "transfer-encoding", "upgrade"})
RESP_STRIP = frozenset({"connection", "keep-alive", "proxy-connection", "te", "trailer", "transfer-encoding",
                        "upgrade", "content-length", "set-cookie"})
HNAME = re.compile(r"[!#$%&'*+.^_`|~0-9A-Za-z-]{1,100}")
HVALUE = re.compile(r"[\t\x20-\x7e\x80-\xff]*")
REASONS = {400: "Bad Request", 403: "Forbidden", 411: "Length Required", 413: "Content Too Large",
           429: "Too Many Requests", 431: "Request Header Fields Too Large", 502: "Bad Gateway",
           503: "Service Unavailable"}


class Proxy:
    """The subject's model API, on a unix socket: see THE PROXY above. One request a connection; each is one line in
    `log`. Every dollar and byte goes through `ledger`, the workspace's for the day; `usd` and `moved` are this run's
    part of it. `fatal` is set, and every later request refused, once the run must end: the day's dollars or bytes are
    gone, or the ledger will not read. The supervisor reads it each tick and kills the run."""
    MAX = 16

    def __init__(self, path, log, ledger, run, cap, cred):
        self.log_path, self.ledger, self.run, self.cred = log, ledger, run, cred
        self.cap_usd, self.cap_bytes = float(cap["SUBJECT_DAILY_USD"]), net_cap(cap)
        self.cap_text = (f"${self.cap_usd:.2f}", f"{cap['SUBJECT_DAILY_NET_MB']:g} MB")
        self.slots, self.lock, self.lines = threading.BoundedSemaphore(self.MAX), threading.Lock(), 0
        self.usd, self.moved, self.left, self.seq = 0.0, 0, 0, 0
        self.fatal, self.stopped = None, False
        self.srv = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
        self.srv.bind(str(path))
        self.srv.listen(16)
        threading.Thread(target=self.serve, daemon=True).start()

    def log(self, **kw):
        with self.lock:
            self.lines += 1
            if self.lines > NET_LOG_LINES + 1:
                return
            if self.lines > NET_LOG_LINES:
                kw = {"note": f"net.log is full at {NET_LOG_LINES} lines; later requests are not recorded"}
            with open(self.log_path, "a") as f:
                f.write(json.dumps({"at": now(), **kw}) + "\n")

    def serve(self):
        while not self.stopped:
            try:
                c, _ = self.srv.accept()
            except OSError:
                return
            if not self.slots.acquire(blocking=False):
                c.close()
                continue
            threading.Thread(target=self.conn, args=(c,), daemon=True).start()

    def conn(self, c):
        try:
            c.settimeout(30)
            self.handle(c)
        except (OSError, ValueError, http.client.HTTPException):
            pass
        finally:
            c.close()
            self.slots.release()

    def die(self, why):
        with self.lock:
            self.fatal = self.fatal or why

    def ledger_broken(self, e):
        self.die(f"killed: the workspace's subject ledger will not read ({e})")

    def take(self, n):
        """Count `n` bytes about to be relayed, taking more from the day's ledger when this run's share is spent;
        False, and the run marked to end, once the day has none left."""
        with self.lock:
            if self.fatal or self.stopped:
                return False
            if self.left < n:
                try:
                    got = self.ledger.take_bytes(n - self.left, self.cap_bytes)
                except LedgerError as e:
                    self.fatal = f"killed: the workspace's subject ledger will not read ({e})"
                    return False
                if not got:
                    self.fatal = f"killed: the workspace's subjects moved the day's {self.cap_text[1]} through the proxy"
                    return False
                self.left += got
            self.left -= n
            self.moved += n
            return True

    def admit(self, fixed, per_out, mt, floor):
        """Hold a request's worst case in the day's ledger (Ledger.hold): (key, "ok", max_tokens held), or (None, v, 0)
        with v "wait" (WAIT_MAX passed with in-flight requests still in the way), "short" or "over" (the run is marked
        to end)."""
        until = time.time() + WAIT_MAX
        while True:
            with self.lock:
                if self.fatal or self.stopped:
                    return None, "over", 0
                self.seq += 1
                key = f"{self.run}/{self.seq}"
                try:
                    v, got = self.ledger.hold(key, fixed, per_out, mt, floor, self.cap_usd)
                except LedgerError as e:
                    self.fatal = f"killed: the workspace's subject ledger will not read ({e})"
                    return None, "over", 0
                if v == "over":
                    self.fatal = f"killed: the workspace's subjects reached the {self.cap_text[0]} daily cap"
                if v == "ok":
                    return key, v, got
                if v != "wait":
                    return None, v, 0
            if time.time() >= until:
                return None, "wait", 0
            time.sleep(WAIT_STEP)

    def settle(self, key, usd):
        try:
            done = self.ledger.settle(key, usd)
        except LedgerError as e:
            self.ledger_broken(e)
            return
        if done:
            with self.lock:
                self.usd += usd

    def refuse(self, c, code, line, why):
        self.log(request=line, allowed=False, status=code, why=why)
        self.error(c, code, why)

    @staticmethod
    def error(c, code, why):
        body = json.dumps({"type": "error", "error": {"type": "cc_subject", "message": why}}).encode()
        c.sendall(f"HTTP/1.1 {code} {REASONS.get(code, 'Error')}\r\nContent-Type: application/json\r\n"
                  f"Content-Length: {len(body)}\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n".encode() + body)

    def handle(self, c):
        head = bytearray()
        while b"\r\n\r\n" not in head:
            if len(head) > HEAD_MAX:
                return self.refuse(c, 431, "", f"a request head is at most {HEAD_MAX} bytes")
            d = c.recv(65536)
            if not d:
                return
            head += d
        raw, _, rest = bytes(head).partition(b"\r\n\r\n")
        lines = raw.decode("latin-1").split("\r\n")
        line = lines[0][:300]
        if len(raw) > HEAD_MAX:
            return self.refuse(c, 431, line, f"a request head is at most {HEAD_MAX} bytes")
        m = re.fullmatch(r"([A-Z]{1,20}) (\S{1,2000}) HTTP/1\.[01]", lines[0])
        method, target = m.groups() if m else ("", "")
        path, _, query = target.partition("?")
        if method != "POST" or path not in API_PATHS or query not in API_QUERIES:
            return self.refuse(c, 403, line, "only POST /v1/messages and /v1/messages/count_tokens go out")
        hdrs = []
        for h in lines[1:]:
            k, sep, v = h.partition(":")
            if not sep or not HNAME.fullmatch(k) or not HVALUE.fullmatch(v):
                return self.refuse(c, 400, line, "a malformed header")
            hdrs.append((k.lower(), v.strip()))
        names = {k for k, _ in hdrs}
        cls = {v for k, v in hdrs if k == "content-length"}
        if "transfer-encoding" in names or len(cls) != 1 or not re.fullmatch(r"\d{1,12}", next(iter(cls))):
            return self.refuse(c, 411, line, "a request needs one Content-Length, and no Transfer-Encoding")
        n = int(next(iter(cls)))
        if n > BODY_MAX:
            return self.refuse(c, 413, line, f"a request body is at most {BODY_MAX} bytes")
        body = bytearray(rest)
        if len(body) > n:
            return self.refuse(c, 400, line, "more bytes than the Content-Length")
        while len(body) < n:
            d = c.recv(min(1 << 20, n - len(body)))
            if not d:
                return
            body += d
        priced = API_PATHS[path]
        ask = parse(bytes(body))
        why = vet(ask, priced) if ask is not None else "the body is not JSON, or nests too deep"
        if why:
            return self.refuse(c, 400 if ask is None else 403, line, why)
        token = read_token(self.cred)
        if token is None:
            return self.refuse(c, 503, line, "the workspace has no usable login")
        if not self.take(len(raw) + 4 + n):
            return self.refuse(c, 403, line, self.fatal or "the run is ending")
        key, r, body, extra = None, 0.0, bytes(body), {}
        if priced:
            counted = self.count(query, hdrs, ask, token)
            fixed, per_out = hold_terms(ask, n, counted)
            mt = ask["max_tokens"]
            key, v, got = self.admit(fixed, per_out, mt, thinking_floor(ask))
            if v == "over":
                return self.refuse(c, 403, line, self.fatal or "the run is ending")
            if v == "wait":
                return self.refuse(c, 429, line, f"the day's dollars are held by requests in flight; waited {WAIT_MAX:g}s")
            if v == "short":
                return self.refuse(c, 429, line, "what is left of the day's dollars will not cover this request at any "
                                                 "max_tokens above its thinking budget")
            r = fixed + got * per_out
            extra = {"counted": counted}
            if got != mt:   # cut to what the day has left: the answer stops at max_tokens, the cap holds
                ask["max_tokens"] = got
                with PARSE:
                    body = json.dumps(ask, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")).encode()
                extra["max_tokens"] = [mt, got]
                if len(body) > n and not self.take(len(body) - n):
                    self.settle(key, 0.0)
                    return self.refuse(c, 403, line, self.fatal or "the run is ending")
        usd, status = r, None   # settled at R unless relay() says otherwise: whatever fails once it is sent was sent
        try:
            usd, status = self.relay(c, target, hdrs, body, ask, r, token)
        finally:
            if key:
                self.settle(key, usd)
            self.log(request=line, allowed=True, status=status, model=ask.get("model"), usd=round(usd, 6), **extra)

    def upstream(self, hdrs, token, n, timeout=UP_TIMEOUT):
        """A connection to UPSTREAM, not yet open, and the headers a request of `n` body bytes goes out with: the
        subject's own less STRIP, the workspace's token, the oauth beta, identity encoding."""
        host, port, tls = UPSTREAM
        out = {k: v for k, v in hdrs if k not in STRIP}
        beta = [b.strip() for b in out.get("anthropic-beta", "").split(",") if b.strip()]
        out.update({"host": host, "authorization": f"Bearer {token}",
                    "anthropic-beta": ",".join(beta + ([] if OAUTH_BETA in beta else [OAUTH_BETA])),
                    "accept-encoding": "identity", "connection": "close", "content-length": str(n)})
        up = (http.client.HTTPSConnection(host, port, timeout=timeout, context=ssl.create_default_context())
              if tls else http.client.HTTPConnection(host, port, timeout=timeout))
        return up, out

    def count(self, query, hdrs, ask, token):
        """The input tokens of a priced request, from the API's free count_tokens, asked with the body cut to
        COUNT_KEYS and the same login; None on any failure, and the hold falls back to the body's estimate. Its bytes
        count against the day like any other."""
        cbody = json.dumps({k: ask[k] for k in COUNT_KEYS if k in ask}, ensure_ascii=False).encode()
        if not self.take(len(cbody)):
            return None
        up, out = self.upstream(hdrs, token, len(cbody), COUNT_TIMEOUT)
        try:
            up.putrequest("POST", "/v1/messages/count_tokens" + (f"?{query}" if query else ""),
                          skip_host=True, skip_accept_encoding=True)
            for k, v in out.items():
                up.putheader(k, v)
            up.endheaders(cbody)
            resp = up.getresponse()
            data = resp.read(1 << 16)
            if not self.take(len(data)) or resp.status != 200:
                return None
            j = parse(data)
            v = j.get("input_tokens") if isinstance(j, dict) else None
            return v if type(v) is int and 0 <= v <= MAX_TOKENS * 10 else None
        except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException, ValueError):
            return None
        finally:
            up.close()

    def relay(self, c, target, hdrs, body, ask, r, token):
        """Send the request upstream with the workspace's token and relay the answer. Returns (dollars, status):
        0 if nothing was sent or the answer is an error; what the usage says if it came whole; else the most of R and
        what was seen."""
        up, out = self.upstream(hdrs, token, len(body))
        try:
            try:
                up.connect()
            except OSError as e:
                try:
                    self.error(c, 502, f"the API did not answer: {e}")
                except OSError:
                    pass
                return 0.0, 502
            try:
                up.putrequest("POST", target, skip_host=True, skip_accept_encoding=True)
                for k, v in out.items():
                    up.putheader(k, v)
                up.endheaders(body)
                resp = up.getresponse()
            except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException, ValueError) as e:
                self.error(c, 502, f"the API dropped the request: {e}")
                return r, 502
            status = resp.status
            meter = Usage("text/event-stream" in (resp.getheader("content-type") or ""))
            rh = "".join(f"{k}: {v}\r\n" for k, v in resp.getheaders() if k.lower() not in RESP_STRIP)
            head = f"HTTP/1.1 {status} {resp.reason}\r\n{rh}Connection: close\r\n\r\n".encode("latin-1", "replace")
            gone = False
            try:
                if self.take(len(head)):
                    c.sendall(head)
                else:
                    gone = True
            except OSError:   # the subject hung up before the answer: the API has done the work all the same
                gone = True
            if not gone:
                while True:
                    try:
                        d = resp.read1(65536)
                    except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
                        break
                    if not d:
                        meter.finish()
                        break
                    meter.feed(d)
                    if not self.take(len(d)):
                        break
                    try:
                        c.sendall(d)
                    except OSError:
                        break
            if status >= 400:
                return 0.0, status
            seen, whole = meter.usd(ask.get("model"))
            if whole and seen is not None:
                return seen, status
            return max(r, seen or 0.0), status
        finally:
            up.close()

    def stop(self):
        """No more requests; the unused part of this run's byte blocks goes back to the day."""
        with self.lock:
            self.stopped = True
            left, self.left = self.left, 0
        self.srv.close()
        try:
            self.ledger.give_bytes(left)
        except LedgerError:
            pass


# The sandbox's first process (pid 2; bwrap's own init is 1). argv: the status fd, then the subject's command. It
# copies /in into /work (a failure, ENOSPC above all, is an "input" line and nothing runs), binds the forwarder BEFORE
# the subject starts, so its first call cannot race the listener, forks the forwarder (loopback to the host's proxy)
# and the subject, and when the subject ends writes "exit N" and waits: the mount namespace, and /work with it, lasts
# until the supervisor has frozen the scope and copied /work out. The status fd never reaches the subject.
INIT = r'''
import os, socket, subprocess, sys, threading, time
st = int(sys.argv[1]); os.set_inheritable(st, False)
def say(s):
    os.write(st, (s.replace("\n", " ")[:400] + "\n").encode())
def hold():
    while True: time.sleep(3600)
if os.path.isdir("/in"):
    p = subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/cp", "-dR", "--preserve=mode,timestamps,links", "--sparse=always", "/in/.", "/work/"],
                       stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
    if p.returncode:
        say("input " + p.stderr.decode(errors="replace").strip()[-300:]); hold()
L = socket.socket(); L.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1); L.bind(("127.0.0.1", %d)); L.listen(32)
if os.fork() == 0:
    os.close(st); os.setsid()
    def pipe(a, b):
        try:
            while True:
                d = a.recv(65536)
                if not d: break
                b.sendall(d)
        except OSError: pass
        for s in (a, b):
            try: s.shutdown(socket.SHUT_RDWR)
            except OSError: pass
    def conn(c):
        u = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX)
        try: u.connect("/run/subject/proxy.sock")
        except OSError: c.close(); return
        threading.Thread(target=pipe, args=(c, u), daemon=True).start(); pipe(u, c)
    while True:
        c, _ = L.accept(); threading.Thread(target=conn, args=(c,), daemon=True).start()
pid = os.fork()
if pid == 0:
    L.close()
    try:
        os.execvp(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[2:])
    except OSError as e:
        os.write(2, ("cc-subject: %%s: %%s\n" %% (sys.argv[2], e.strerror)).encode())
    os._exit(127)
L.close()
_, ws = os.waitpid(pid, 0)
say("exit %%d" %% os.waitstatus_to_exitcode(ws))
hold()
''' % PROXY_PORT


def claude_binary():
    p = os.path.realpath(os.environ.get("CC_CLAUDE") or REALHOME / ".local/bin/claude")
    return p if os.path.isfile(p) else None


def unit(run):
    return f"cc-subject-{run}"


def boundary(rd, cmd, net, disk_mb, status_fd, info_fd):
    """The argv for the subject of run dir `rd` whose proxy socket is in `net`: a scope named for the run, and in it a
    bwrap that writes its child's pid to `info_fd` and whose first process reports on `status_fd`. Also the
    descriptors bwrap reads (passwd, group, hosts)."""
    uid, gid = os.getuid(), os.getgid()
    files = [f"subject:x:{uid}:{gid}:subject:/home/subject:/bin/bash\n", f"subject:x:{gid}:\n",
             "127.0.0.1 localhost\n::1 localhost\n"]
    fds = []
    for text in files:
        r, w = os.pipe()
        os.write(w, text.encode())
        os.close(w)
        fds.append(r)
    b = ["bwrap", "--die-with-parent", "--unshare-all", "--new-session", "--clearenv", "--hostname", "subject",
         "--info-fd", str(info_fd), "--ro-bind", "/usr", "/usr", "--symlink", "usr/bin", "/bin", "--symlink", "usr/lib", "/lib",
         "--symlink", "usr/lib64", "/lib64", "--symlink", "usr/sbin", "/sbin",
         "--tmpfs", "/etc"]
    for e in ("ld.so.cache", "ssl/certs", "ssl/openssl.cnf", "ca-certificates", "alternatives", "localtime"):
        b += ["--ro-bind-try", f"/etc/{e}", f"/etc/{e}"]
    b += ["--file", str(fds[0]), "/etc/passwd", "--file", str(fds[1]), "/etc/group", "--file", str(fds[2]), "/etc/hosts",
          "--proc", "/proc", "--dev", "/dev", "--size", str(TMP_BYTES), "--tmpfs", "/tmp", "--tmpfs", "/run",
          "--ro-bind", str(net), "/run/subject",
          "--size", str(HOME_BYTES), "--tmpfs", "/home/subject", "--size", str(int(disk_mb) << 20), "--tmpfs", "/work"]
    if (rd / "in").is_dir():
        b += ["--ro-bind", str(rd / "in"), "/in"]
    b += ["--chdir", "/work"]
    path = "/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"
    cb = claude_binary()
    if cb:
        b += ["--ro-bind", cb, "/opt/subject/bin/claude"]
        path = "/opt/subject/bin:" + path
    # No credential and no proxy variable: the API is at 127.0.0.1, and the proxy behind it puts the login on
    env = {"HOME": "/home/subject", "USER": "subject", "PATH": path, "TMPDIR": "/tmp", "LANG": "C.UTF-8",
           "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": f"http://127.0.0.1:{PROXY_PORT}", "CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN": "subject-placeholder",
           "CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC": "1", "CC_SUBJECT_RUN": rd.name}
    for k, v in env.items():
        b += ["--setenv", k, v]
    scope = ["systemd-run", "--user", "--scope", "--quiet", "--unit", unit(rd.name), "-p", f"MemoryMax={MEMORY}",
             "-p", "MemorySwapMax=0", "-p", f"TasksMax={TASKS}", "--", "prlimit", f"--fsize={FILE_BYTES}:{FILE_BYTES}", "--"]
    return scope + b + ["--", "/usr/bin/python3", "-I", "-c", INIT, str(status_fd)] + list(cmd), fds


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the sandbox's /work, live and kept

def scope_of(pid, run):
    """The cgroup path of process `pid` if it is in run `run`'s own scope, else None."""
    try:
        with open(f"/proc/{int(pid)}/cgroup") as f:
            lines = f.read().splitlines()
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return None
    cg = next((x[3:] for x in lines if x.startswith("0::")), "")
    return cg if cg.endswith(f"/{unit(run)}.scope") and "/../" not in cg else None


def cgroup_write(cg, name, value):
    try:
        with open(f"/sys/fs/cgroup{cg}/{name}", "w") as f:
            f.write(value)
        return True
    except OSError:
        return False


def freeze(cg):
    """Freeze the cgroup `cg`; True only once the kernel says it is frozen."""
    if not cgroup_write(cg, "cgroup.freeze", "1"):
        return False
    until = time.time() + FREEZE_WAIT
    while time.time() < until:
        try:
            with open(f"/sys/fs/cgroup{cg}/cgroup.events") as f:
                if "frozen 1" in f.read().splitlines():
                    return True
        except OSError:
            return False
        time.sleep(0.05)
    return False


def live_work(pid, run):
    """An fd on the live /work of run `run`'s sandbox, whose first pid is `pid`, or None. It is opened first and the
    scope checked after, so a pid that was reused before the open is caught by the check."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(f"/proc/{int(pid)}/root/work", os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return None
    if scope_of(pid, run) is None:
        os.close(fd)
        return None
    return fd


def normalise(root):
    """Make every dir under `root` 0700 and every file 0600, or 0700 if it was executable, no set-id bit, before the
    host reads, keeps or removes it. Nothing is followed: a link is left as it is, and only what lstat calls a dir is
    entered. `root` is a tree only the host writes by now (a copy the subject cannot reach, or the run's in/)."""
    try:
        if not stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(root).st_mode):
            return
        os.chmod(root, 0o700)
    except OSError:
        return
    for _top, dirs, names, dfd in os.fwalk(root, follow_symlinks=False):
        for n in dirs + names:
            try:
                m = os.stat(n, dir_fd=dfd, follow_symlinks=False).st_mode
                if stat.S_ISLNK(m):
                    continue
                os.chmod(n, 0o700 if stat.S_ISDIR(m) or (stat.S_ISREG(m) and m & 0o111) else 0o600, dir_fd=dfd)
            except OSError:
                pass


def prune(p):
    """Remove `p`, a dir of a run's: normalised first, so a dir the subject made unreadable cannot stop it."""
    try:
        if stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(p).st_mode):
            normalise(p)
            shutil.rmtree(p)
        else:
            os.unlink(p)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    except OSError:
        traceback.print_exc()


def walk(dfd, visit):
    """Hand every entry of the tree under the dir open on `dfd` to visit(rel, entry), `rel` the path of the entry's dir
    from the top ("" at the top) and `entry` its os.DirEntry; visit returns True to stop the walk there. Only what
    scandir calls a dir without following is entered, each one opened from its parent's fd O_NOFOLLOW, so a link is
    handed over as a link and never stat'd through or opened: in a live /work an absolute link would resolve against
    the host's root. A dir that will not open or list raises its OSError, never skips its subtree, and that includes
    the EMFILE a chain deeper than the fd limit hits, since the walk holds an fd a level. Every fd is closed after."""
    fds, rels, todo, stop = [], [], [], False

    def scan(fd, rel):
        nonlocal stop
        out = []
        with os.scandir(fd) as it:
            for e in it:
                if visit(rel, e):
                    stop = True
                    break
                if e.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False):
                    out.append(e.name)
        return out

    try:
        fds.append(os.dup(dfd))
        rels.append("")
        todo.append(scan(fds[-1], ""))
        while todo and not stop:
            if not todo[-1]:
                todo.pop()
                rels.pop()
                os.close(fds.pop())
                continue
            name = todo[-1].pop()
            fds.append(os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=fds[-1]))
            rels.append(f"{rels[-1]}/{name}" if rels[-1] else name)
            todo.append(scan(fds[-1], rels[-1]))
    finally:
        for fd in fds:
            os.close(fd)


def count_entries(dfd, limit):
    """True if the tree under the dir open on `dfd` holds `limit` entries or fewer, else a str saying why not. A link
    is counted and never followed, and any dir walk() cannot open or list refuses the whole count."""
    n = 0

    def visit(_rel, _e):
        nonlocal n
        n += 1
        return n > limit

    try:
        walk(dfd, visit)
    except OSError as e:
        return f"/work could not be counted ({e.strerror})"
    return True if n <= limit else f"/work holds more than {limit} files and dirs"


def copy_out(pid, run, dst):
    """Copy the frozen sandbox's /work to `dst`, a new dir, then normalise it; a /work of more than WORK_ENTRIES
    entries, or one count_entries cannot walk to the end, is not copied at all. cp works through /proc/self/fd of dir
    fds opened O_NOFOLLOW on both sides and copies a link as a link (-d), so nothing it writes or reads is outside
    the two trees. True, or a str saying what went wrong (what was copied stays)."""
    src = live_work(pid, run)
    if src is None:
        return "the sandbox's /work could not be opened"
    n = count_entries(src, WORK_ENTRIES)   # empty files cost the tmpfs nothing but each costs the host an inode
    if n is not True:
        os.close(src)
        return f"{n}, so none of it was copied"
    try:
        os.mkdir(dst, 0o700)
        out = os.open(dst, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError as e:
        os.close(src)
        return f"{dst} could not be made: {e.strerror}"
    try:
        p = sp.run(["/usr/bin/cp", "-dR", "--preserve=timestamps,links", "--sparse=always",
                    f"/proc/self/fd/{src}/.", f"/proc/self/fd/{out}/"], pass_fds=(src, out), stdin=sp.DEVNULL,
                   capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=COPY_WAIT)
        return True if p.returncode == 0 else f"the copy out failed: {p.stderr.strip()[-200:]}"
    except sp.TimeoutExpired:
        return f"the copy out took longer than {COPY_WAIT}s"
    finally:
        os.close(src)
        os.close(out)
        normalise(dst)


def end_sandbox(p, pid, cg, run, dst, keep):
    """End the sandbox of `p`, whose first pid is `pid` and whose scope is the cgroup `cg`: freeze it, copy its /work to
    `dst` if `keep`, kill the cgroup and the process group. A scope that will not confirm it is frozen is killed with
    nothing copied. Returns None, or a note on why the results were not (all) kept."""
    note = None
    if p.poll() is None and cg:
        if not freeze(cg):
            note = "results not kept: the sandbox did not freeze"
        elif keep and pid:
            done = copy_out(pid, run, dst)
            note = None if done is True else f"results not fully kept: {done}"
        cgroup_write(cg, "cgroup.kill", "1")
    elif keep:
        note = "results not kept: the sandbox had already gone"
    try:
        os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
    except OSError:
        pass
    p.wait()
    return note


def read_info(fd, p):
    """The pid bwrap names on its --info-fd, once it parses; an error if bwrap ends or INFO_WAIT passes first."""
    buf, until = b"", time.time() + INFO_WAIT
    while time.time() < until:
        if select.select([fd], [], [], 0.5)[0]:
            d = os.read(fd, 4096)
            if not d:
                break
            buf += d
            try:
                return int(json.loads(buf)["child-pid"])
            except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
                continue
        elif p.poll() is not None:
            break
    raise RuntimeError("the sandbox did not start" + (f" (exit {p.poll()})" if p.poll() is not None else ""))


def stamp_time(v):
    try:
        return calendar.timegm(time.strptime(str(v), "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"))
    except ValueError:
        return None


def sweep(h, keep_days):
    """Prune what ended runs older than `keep_days` keep on disk (work/, in/, home/, cred/), and delete ledger files of
    days older than that. A live run, or one whose stamps will not read, is left whole. The in/ of any run that is
    not live goes whatever its age: a launcher killed in the middle of the copy leaves a partial one behind."""
    cut = time.time() - float(keep_days) * 86400
    for run, st in runs_of(h):
        if state_of(st) in LIVE:
            continue
        prune(subjects(h) / run / "in")
        t = stamp_time(st.get("ended") or st.get("started"))
        if t is not None and t < cut:
            for d in ("work", "in", "home", "cred"):
                prune(subjects(h) / run / d)
    led = subjects(h) / "ledger"
    day = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d", time.gmtime(cut))
    for f in led.iterdir() if led.is_dir() else []:
        m = re.fullmatch(r"(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})\.json", f.name)
        if m and m.group(1) < day:
            prune(f)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ launch (the daemon's door)

def tree_ok(h, path):
    """(the real directory `path` names, "") if it is inside one of this workspace's own trees, else (None, why)."""
    if not isinstance(path, str) or not path.startswith("/") or "\0" in path:
        return None, "--in takes an absolute path inside the workspace"
    real = os.path.realpath(path)
    if real != os.path.normpath(path):
        return None, f"{path} passes through a link; name the directory itself"
    roots = [os.path.realpath(HOME / "dev" / h), os.path.realpath(HOME / ".cc/worktrees" / h)]
    if not any(real == r or real.startswith(r + "/") for r in roots):
        return None, f"{path} is not inside workspace {h}'s own trees"
    if not os.path.isdir(real):
        return None, f"{path} is not a directory"
    return real, ""


def tree_bytes(top, dir_fd=None, limit=None):
    """The disk a tree takes, in bytes of st_blocks but at least ENTRY_BYTES an entry, so a tree of empty files is
    not free: `top` itself and everything under it, lstat'd and walked by walk(), so a link counts as a link and
    nothing it names is reached. `top` is a path, or "." with `dir_fd` a descriptor on the dir; a `top` that is not
    there takes 0. A dir under it that will not open or list raises its OSError, so a cap built on this refuses
    rather than skipping what it could not see. With `limit`, the count stops once it is past it."""
    try:
        st = os.stat(top, dir_fd=dir_fd, follow_symlinks=False)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return 0
    n = max(st.st_blocks * 512, ENTRY_BYTES)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode):
        return n

    def visit(_rel, e):
        nonlocal n
        try:
            n += max(e.stat(follow_symlinks=False).st_blocks * 512, ENTRY_BYTES)
        except FileNotFoundError:   # gone since it was listed: it takes nothing now
            pass
        return limit is not None and n > limit

    fd = os.open(top, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dir_fd)
    try:
        walk(fd, visit)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    return n


def copy_in(src, dst, limit):
    """Copy the directory `src` into `dst` from inside a bwrap that sees only those two: the source is opened
    here and handed over as a descriptor, so nothing resolves its name a second time, and a link in it is copied as
    a link — it points into a world where there is nothing to reach. A source past `limit` bytes is refused before
    anything is copied, counted through that descriptor; `dst` is measured while the copy runs and after, so a
    source that grows meanwhile is stopped too. A tree with a dir that will not open or list cannot be measured, so
    it is refused too. True, or a str saying what went wrong."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(src, os.O_PATH | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError as e:
        return f"cannot open {src}: {e.strerror}"
    too_big = f"{src} takes more than the {limit >> 20} MB a run's /work holds (SUBJECT_DISK_MB)"

    def over(top, dir_fd=None):
        try:
            return too_big if tree_bytes(top, dir_fd, limit) > limit else None
        except OSError as e:
            return f"{src} could not be measured against SUBJECT_DISK_MB ({e.strerror}), so it is not copied"

    try:
        if os.readlink(f"/proc/self/fd/{fd}") != src:
            return f"{src} moved while it was being opened"
        why = over(".", fd)
        if why:
            return why
        b = ["bwrap", "--die-with-parent", "--unshare-all", "--new-session", "--clearenv",
             "--ro-bind", "/usr", "/usr", "--symlink", "usr/bin", "/bin", "--symlink", "usr/lib", "/lib",
             "--symlink", "usr/lib64", "/lib64", "--proc", "/proc", "--dev", "/dev",
             "--ro-bind-fd", str(fd), "/src", "--bind", str(dst), "/dst", "--",
             "/usr/bin/cp", "-a", "--no-preserve=ownership", "/src/.", "/dst/"]
        p = sp.Popen(b, pass_fds=(fd,), stdin=sp.DEVNULL, stdout=sp.DEVNULL, stderr=sp.PIPE, text=True)
        until, err = time.time() + COPY_WAIT, ""
        while True:
            try:
                err = p.communicate(timeout=1)[1] or ""
                break
            except sp.TimeoutExpired:
                why = over(dst) or (f"the copy took longer than {COPY_WAIT}s" if time.time() > until else None)
                if why:
                    p.kill()
                    p.communicate()
                    return why
        why = over(dst)
        if why:
            return why
        return True if p.returncode == 0 else f"the copy failed: {err.strip()[-200:]}"
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def start(h, ask, cap, spawn=True):
    """Make a run for workspace `h` and start its supervisor. Returns the JSON answer."""
    argv, src, hours = ask.get("argv"), ask.get("input") or "", ask.get("hours")
    hours = min(2, cap["SUBJECT_MAX_HOURS"]) if hours is None else hours
    if not isinstance(argv, list) or not argv or not all(isinstance(a, str) and "\0" not in a for a in argv):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "a run needs a command"}
    if not isinstance(hours, (int, float)) or not 0 < hours <= cap["SUBJECT_MAX_HOURS"]:
        return {"ok": False, "error": f"--hours must be above 0 and at most {cap['SUBJECT_MAX_HOURS']:g}"}
    for tool in ("bwrap", "systemd-run", "prlimit"):
        if not shutil.which(tool):
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"{tool} is not on the host, so there is no sandbox to run a subject in"}
    if src:
        src, why = tree_ok(h, src)
        if why:
            return {"ok": False, "error": why}
    why = login_why(h)
    if why:
        return {"ok": False, "error": why}
    root = subjects(h)
    root.mkdir(mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    with open(root / ".lock", "a") as lk:
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        sweep(h, cap["SUBJECT_KEEP_DAYS"])
        most = int(cap["SUBJECT_KEPT_MB"]) << 20
        try:
            kept = tree_bytes(root, limit=most)
        except OSError as e:   # what it cannot see might be past the cap, so no run starts
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h}'s kept subject results could not be measured against "
                                          f"SUBJECT_KEPT_MB ({e.strerror}), so no run starts"}
        if kept > most:   # refused before the run dir is made: it is not one of the day's
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h}'s kept subject results take more than the "
                                          f"{cap['SUBJECT_KEPT_MB']:g} MB it may keep (SUBJECT_KEPT_MB); "
                                          f"they go after {cap['SUBJECT_KEEP_DAYS']:g} days, so no run starts until then"}
        _, live = day_totals(h, today())
        try:
            led = Ledger(h, today()).read()
        except LedgerError as e:
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h}'s subject ledger for today will not read ({e}), so no run starts"}
        usd, net = led["usd"] + sum(led["held"].values()), led["bytes"]
        if usd >= cap["SUBJECT_DAILY_USD"]:
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h}'s subjects have spent ${usd:.2f} today, the cap is ${cap['SUBJECT_DAILY_USD']:.2f}"}
        if net >= net_cap(cap):
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h}'s subjects have moved {net / (1 << 20):.1f} MB through the "
                                          f"proxy today, the cap is {cap['SUBJECT_DAILY_NET_MB']:g} MB"}
        if live >= cap["SUBJECT_CONCURRENT"]:
            return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h} already has {live} subject runs going, the most at once"}
        run = time.strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S", time.gmtime()) + "-" + secrets.token_hex(3)
        rd = root / run
        rd.mkdir(mode=0o700)
        if src:
            (rd / "in").mkdir(mode=0o700)
        # `supervisor` is the process that will end this run: this one while it copies, the supervisor once spawned
        st = {"run": run, "argv": argv, "input": src, "hours": hours, "state": "starting", "started": now(), "usd": 0.0,
              "supervisor": os.getpid()}
        write_json(rd / "status.json", st)
    if src:
        ok = copy_in(src, rd / "in", int(cap["SUBJECT_DISK_MB"]) << 20)
        if ok is not True:   # counted all the same, so a copy that fails cannot be retried without end
            prune(rd / "in")
            write_json(rd / "status.json", {**st, "state": "failed", "ended": now(), "why": ok})
            return {"ok": False, "error": ok}
    if spawn:
        with open(rd / "supervise.log", "ab") as log, open(root / ".lock", "a") as lk:
            fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)   # the supervisor takes this lock to write its own pid: no lost update
            try:
                p = sp.Popen(supervisor_argv(h, run), stdin=sp.DEVNULL, stdout=log, stderr=log, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
            except OSError as e:
                prune(rd / "in")
                write_json(rd / "status.json", {**st, "state": "failed", "ended": now(), "why": f"failed: {e}"})
                return {"ok": False, "error": f"the supervisor did not start: {e}"}
            cur = read_json(rd / "status.json", {})
            if cur.get("state") == "starting" and cur.get("supervisor") == os.getpid():
                write_json(rd / "status.json", {**cur, "supervisor": p.pid})
    return {"ok": True, "run": run, "text": f"subject run {run} started; `cc-subject status {run}` reads it"}


def supervisor_argv(h, run):
    """The supervisor in a scope of its own, so the request bodies it parses are bounded by its own memory cap. A
    --scope systemd-run execs the command in place: the pid Popen sees is the supervisor's."""
    return ["systemd-run", "--user", "--scope", "--quiet", "-p", f"MemoryMax={SUPERVISOR_MEMORY}",
            "-p", "MemorySwapMax=0", "--", sys.executable, "-I", str(Path(__file__).resolve()), "supervise", h, run]


def net_cap(cap):
    return int(float(cap["SUBJECT_DAILY_NET_MB"]) * (1 << 20))


def stop(h, run):
    if not isinstance(run, str) or not RUN.fullmatch(run) or not (subjects(h) / run).is_dir():
        return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h} has no subject run {run}"}
    st = read_json(subjects(h) / run / "status.json", {})
    if state_of(st) not in LIVE:
        why = "; its supervisor ended without recording an end" if st.get("state") in LIVE else ""
        return {"ok": False, "error": f"run {run} is not going ({state_of(st)}{why})"}
    (subjects(h) / run / "stop").touch()
    return {"ok": True, "text": f"run {run} will stop within {TICK:g}s"}


def row(run, st):
    return (f"{run}  {state_of(st) or '?':8}  ${float(st.get('usd') or 0):.2f}  {int(st.get('net_bytes') or 0) / (1 << 20):.1f}MB  "
            f"{' '.join(map(str, st.get('argv') or []))[:80]}"
            + (f"  ({st['why']})" if st.get("why") else ""))


def tail(p, n=TAIL_LINES):
    try:
        with open(p, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(max(0, os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_size - 64 * 1024))
            return f.read().decode(errors="replace").splitlines()[-n:]
    except OSError:
        return []


def open_under(dfd, rel):
    """An fd for the regular file `rel` under the dir fd `dfd`, every component opened with O_NOFOLLOW from the one
    before, so a link the subject planted reaches nothing outside its own /work. None when any part is not there or
    not plain, or the path will not do as one (a NUL byte in it)."""
    parts = [x for x in rel.split("/") if x not in ("", ".")]
    if not parts or ".." in parts:
        return None
    fds = []
    try:
        cur = dfd
        for x in parts[:-1]:
            cur = os.open(x, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=cur)
            fds.append(cur)
        fd = os.open(parts[-1], os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=cur)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):
            os.close(fd)
            return None
        return fd
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    finally:
        for d in fds:
            os.close(d)


def work_fd(rd, run, st):
    """(fd on the run's /work, "live" or "kept"), or (None, why not): a live run's own /work through /proc, else the
    copy the end left in the run dir."""
    if state_of(st) in LIVE and st.get("sandbox"):
        fd = live_work(st["sandbox"], run)
        if fd is not None:
            return fd, "live"
    try:
        return os.open(rd / "work", os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC), "kept"
    except OSError:
        return None, ("not there yet" if state_of(st) in LIVE else "not kept")


def login_line(st):
    exp = st.get("login_expires")
    if not isinstance(exp, str):
        return []
    if exp <= now():
        return [f"workspace login: expired at {exp}; calls get 401 until a session in the workspace renews it"]
    return [f"workspace login: expires at {exp}"]


def status(h, run=None, path=None):
    """The workspace's only view of its runs: they are never bound into it."""
    if run is None:
        return {"ok": True, "text": "\n".join(row(r, st) for r, st in runs_of(h)) or "no subject runs yet"}
    if not isinstance(run, str) or not RUN.fullmatch(run) or not (subjects(h) / run).is_dir():
        return {"ok": False, "error": f"workspace {h} has no subject run {run}"}
    rd = subjects(h) / run
    st = read_json(rd / "status.json", {})
    st = st if isinstance(st, dict) else {}
    wfd, how = work_fd(rd, run, st)
    try:
        if path is not None:
            path = str(path)
            path = path[len("/work/"):] if path.startswith("/work/") else path   # the form the usage text names
            fd = open_under(wfd, path) if wfd is not None else None
            if fd is None:
                return {"ok": False, "error": f"run {run} has no regular file /work/{path.replace(chr(0), '?')}"}
            with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
                data = f.read(READ_BYTES + 1)
            more = f"\n[cut at {READ_BYTES} bytes]" if len(data) > READ_BYTES else ""
            return {"ok": True, "text": data[:READ_BYTES].decode(errors="replace") + more}
        files, cut = [], ""

        def visit(rel, e):   # a link is listed as one and never stat'd: in a live /work it would resolve on the host
            if e.is_symlink():
                files.append(f"{rel}/{e.name}".lstrip("/") + " (link)")
            elif not e.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False):
                files.append(f"{rel}/{e.name}".lstrip("/"))
            return len(files) > LIST_MAX

        try:
            if wfd is not None:
                walk(wfd, visit)
        except OSError as e:
            cut = f"; a dir would not open or list ({e.strerror}), so the list stops there"
        files.sort()
    finally:
        if wfd is not None:
            os.close(wfd)
    out = [row(run, st), *login_line(st), "", "out.log (tail):", *tail(rd / "out.log"),
           "", "net.log (tail):", *tail(rd / "net.log"), ""]
    if st.get("results"):
        out.append(st["results"])
    out += [f"/work, {how} ({len(files[:LIST_MAX])} files" + (", list cut" if len(files) > LIST_MAX else "") + cut + "):",
            *files[:LIST_MAX]]
    return {"ok": True, "text": "\n".join(out)}


def launch(h, ask):
    if not isinstance(h, str) or not HANDLE.fullmatch(h) or not member_dir(h).is_dir():
        return {"ok": False, "error": f"{h} is not a member workspace"}
    if not isinstance(ask, dict):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "an ask is a JSON object"}
    if ask.get("op") == "run":
        return start(h, ask, caps())
    if ask.get("op") == "stop":
        return stop(h, ask.get("run"))
    if ask.get("op") == "status":
        return status(h, ask.get("run"), ask.get("path"))
    return {"ok": False, "error": "op is run, stop or status"}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ supervise

def supervise(h, run, cap=None):
    """Run the subject of `run` to its end. Whatever goes wrong in here — a command the kernel will not exec, a
    socket that will not bind, an input too big for /work, a ledger that will not read — the finally ends the sandbox
    (freeze, keep /work, kill: see THE END above), stops the proxy, settles what the run left in flight, removes the
    socket and the run's in/, and writes a terminal state, so a run is never left marked live with nothing to end it."""
    cap = cap or caps()
    rd = subjects(h) / run
    net, proxy, p, ledger, why, state, st = sock_dir(h, run), None, None, None, "", None, {"run": run}
    pid, cg, rfd, code, keep = None, None, None, None, True
    try:
        with open(rd.parent / ".lock", "a") as lk:   # start() writes the spawned pid under this lock: take it over
            fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            st = read_json(rd / "status.json")
            if not isinstance(st, dict):
                st = {"run": run}
                raise ValueError("status.json is unreadable")
            st["supervisor"] = os.getpid()
            write_json(rd / "status.json", st)
        make_sock_dir(net)
        ledger = Ledger(h, str(st["started"])[:10])   # the day the run started pays for all of it
        proxy = Proxy(net / "proxy.sock", rd / "net.log", ledger, run, cap, member_dir(h) / "credentials.json")
        rfd, wfd = os.pipe()
        ifr, ifw = os.pipe()
        os.set_blocking(rfd, False)
        argv, fds = boundary(rd, st["argv"], net, cap["SUBJECT_DISK_MB"], wfd, ifw)
        try:
            with open(rd / "out.log", "ab") as out:
                p = sp.Popen(argv, pass_fds=fds + [wfd, ifw], stdin=sp.DEVNULL, stdout=out, stderr=out,
                             start_new_session=True)
        finally:
            for fd in fds + [wfd, ifw] + ([ifr] if p is None else []):
                os.close(fd)
        try:
            pid = read_info(ifr, p)
        finally:
            os.close(ifr)
        cg = scope_of(pid, run)
        if cg is None:
            raise RuntimeError(f"the sandbox is not in its own scope {unit(run)}")
        deadline = time.time() + float(st["hours"]) * 3600
        st.update(sandbox=pid, login_expires=login_expires(h))
        write_json(rd / "status.json", {**st, "state": "running"})
        buf = b""
        while True:
            try:
                while True:
                    d = os.read(rfd, 4096)
                    if not d:
                        break
                    buf += d
            except BlockingIOError:
                pass
            line = buf.split(b"\n", 1)[0].decode(errors="replace") if b"\n" in buf else ""
            if line.startswith("exit "):
                code = int(line[5:]) if re.fullmatch(r"-?\d{1,4}", line[5:]) else None
                break
            if line.startswith("input"):
                why, keep = f"failed: the input did not copy into /work:{line[5:]}", False
            elif line:
                why = f"failed: the sandbox said {line[:100]!r}"
            elif p.poll() is not None:
                why = "failed: the sandbox ended before its subject did"
            elif proxy.fatal:
                why = proxy.fatal
            elif time.time() > deadline:
                why = f"killed: past its {float(st['hours']):g} hours"
            elif (rd / "stop").exists():
                why = "stopped on request"
            if why:
                break
            time.sleep(TICK)
            st.update(usd=round(proxy.usd, 6), net_bytes=proxy.moved, login_expires=login_expires(h))
            write_json(rd / "status.json", {**st, "state": "running"})
        if not why and proxy.fatal:   # the subject ended on its own after the proxy refused it for good
            why = proxy.fatal
        state = why.split(":")[0] if why.startswith(("killed", "failed")) else "stopped" if why else "done"
    except BaseException as e:   # SystemExit too: main() turns SIGTERM into one
        traceback.print_exc()
        first = (str(e).strip().splitlines() or [""])[0][:200]
        why, state = f"failed: {type(e).__name__}{': ' + first if first else ''}", "failed"
    finally:
        if p is not None:
            try:
                note = end_sandbox(p, pid, cg, run, rd / "work", keep)
            except BaseException as e:   # still kill: the results are lost, the sandbox must not outlive this
                traceback.print_exc()
                note = f"results not kept: {type(e).__name__}"
                if cg:
                    cgroup_write(cg, "cgroup.kill", "1")
                with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                    os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
                p.wait()
            if note:
                st["results"] = note
        if rfd is not None:
            os.close(rfd)
        if proxy is not None:
            proxy.stop()
            try:
                left = ledger.release_run(run)   # what is still in flight is spent at its worst case
            except LedgerError:
                traceback.print_exc()
                left = 0.0
            st["usd"], st["net_bytes"] = round(proxy.usd + left, 6), proxy.moved
        try:
            (net / "proxy.sock").unlink()   # a host-only path: nothing the subject wrote
        except OSError:
            pass
        try:
            net.rmdir()
        except OSError:
            pass
        prune(rd / "in")
        st.update(state=state or "failed", ended=now(), exit=code, why=why)
        write_json(rd / "status.json", st)
    return st


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ inside a member workspace

def ask_host(ask, timeout=360):
    c = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    c.settimeout(timeout)
    try:
        c.connect(str(REALHOME / ".cc/slack/sock"))
        c.sendall((json.dumps({"subject": ask}) + "\n").encode())
        buf = b""
        while not buf.endswith(b"\n"):
            d = c.recv(65536)
            if not d:
                break
            buf += d
    finally:
        c.close()
    return json.loads(buf or b"{}")


def inside(args):
    if args[:1] == ["status"] and len(args) <= 3:
        ask = {"op": "status", **dict(zip(("run", "path"), args[1:]))}
    elif args[:1] == ["stop"] and len(args) == 2:
        ask = {"op": "stop", "run": args[1]}
    elif args[:1] == ["run"] and "--" in args:
        opts, cmd = args[1:args.index("--")], args[args.index("--") + 1:]
        ask = {"op": "run", "argv": cmd}
        while opts:
            if opts[0] == "--in" and len(opts) > 1:
                ask["input"] = os.path.abspath(opts[1])
            elif opts[0] == "--hours" and len(opts) > 1:
                try:
                    ask["hours"] = float(opts[1])
                except ValueError:
                    return usage()
            else:
                return usage()
            opts = opts[2:]
    else:
        return usage()
    try:
        res = ask_host(ask)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"cc-subject: the host did not answer ({e})", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(res.get("text") or res.get("error") or res, file=sys.stdout if res.get("ok") else sys.stderr)
    return 0 if res.get("ok") else 1


def usage():
    print(__doc__[__doc__.index("usage, INSIDE"):], file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


def main(args):
    if args[:1] in (["--help"], ["-h"]):
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    if os.environ.get("CC_MEMBER_SANDBOX") == "1":
        return inside(args)
    if args == ["selfcheck"]:
        return runpy.run_path(str(BIN.parent / "tests/subject.py"))["selfcheck"](sys.modules[__name__])
    if len(args) == 2 and args[0] == "launch":
        try:
            ask = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(1 << 20) or "null")
        except ValueError:
            ask = None
        print(json.dumps(launch(args[1], ask)))
        return 0
    if len(args) == 2 and args[0] == "list" and HANDLE.fullmatch(args[1]):
        print(status(args[1])["text"])
        return 0
    if len(args) == 3 and args[0] == "supervise" and HANDLE.fullmatch(args[1]) and RUN.fullmatch(args[2]):
        signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: sys.exit("terminated"))   # so the finally in supervise() runs
        supervise(args[1], args[2])
        return 0
    return usage()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
